      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In experiments on rats it was shown that administration of succinic and nicotinic acids in doses of 30 and 4 mg/kg for 5 days elevated pyruvic acid level and changed catecholamine balance in tissues of the aorta and heart. The administration of the drugs to rats with current-induced stress partially eliminated unfavourable shifts in carbohydrate metabolism and catecholamine balance in the aortic and cardiac tissues. Succinic acid had more pronounced metabolic activity."},
